<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santiago Méndez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1798">1798</a>–<a href="/years/1872">1872</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> Méndez <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibarra">Ibarra</a> was a politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a> who served several times as governor of Yucatán in the 1840s and 1850s. He led the Campeche faction in a long rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miguel-barbachano">Miguel Barbachano</a> of Mérida. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">Caste</a> War in 1848 he offered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over Yucatán to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in return for help against the Maya rebels.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santiago-mendez.jpg" alt="Santiago Méndez" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santiago_Mendez_12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
